    "asOf": "2026-10-14",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Nick Schultz has represented the 44th District in the California State Assembly since December 2024. He previously served as Burbank mayor and a state prosecutor of public corruption, officer-involved shootings and financial fraud. He chairs the Assembly Committee on Public Safety and serves on the Budget, Natural Resources, and Utilities and Energy committees.",
        "cites": [1, 2],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Nick Schultz has represented the 44th District in the California State Assembly since December 2024.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He previously served as Burbank mayor and a state prosecutor of public corruption, officer-involved shootings and financial fraud.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He chairs the Assembly Committee on Public Safety and serves on the Budget, Natural Resources, and Utilities and Energy committees.",
            "cites": [2]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In 2026, his bills became law requiring prosecutors to justify refiling dismissed charges, mandating PFAS disclosure in pesticides, and restricting undercover interrogations of young people. He called for oversight hearings on heat conditions at Donovan state prison. He has made supporting the American film industry an Assembly priority.",
        "cites": [3, 4, 2]
      }
    ]
  },
